When handling an issue, we have to think first like a QA.

Describe what we have in code now and what it does.

Example:

Description: Email sending module, that sends emails to users passed in params.
Actual: Not sending email.
Expected: It should send email to user.

ULTRA IMPORTANT: Always analyze our code to see whats actual then compare it against whats expected.

Make a comparision table that shows the code that is fauly and what it shouuld be in order to work as expected.
